Prospective scope only. No new numerical result is claimed here.

## Evidence inherited from w008

- The released Nyström `1e-12` singular-value floor was entered in 135/448 frozen native spectrum rows, concentrated at `k >= 140`.
- In the four outcome-informed native cases tested, released versus alternative spectral mappings produced no strict permutation-score pair reversal and no binary decision change; the largest score-vector relative L2 difference was `6.382908e-6`.
- The released RFF implementation draws `R` frequencies but materializes `2R` cosine/sine coordinates. Reusing one integer seed across different `R` values does not pair permutation rows because feature sampling advances the same RNG first.

